quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  18,35,And he went into his garden wronging himself (by way of arrogance). He said: ‘I do not think that this will ever perish.
  18,36,"And I do not think that the Hour will ever come. And even if I am returned to my Lord, I will surely find a resort better than this.’"
  18,37,"His companion said to him while conversing with him: ‘Do you disbelieve in Him Who created you (i.e. your father Adam) from dust, and then (developed you) from a zygote*, and then fashioned you as a man?"
  18,38,"But He is Allah, my Lord, and I do not ascribe any partner to my Lord."
  18,39,"And why did you not say when you entered your garden: ‘(This is) what Allah has willed! There is no power except in Allah!’ If you see that I am lesser than you in wealth and children,"
  18,40,"perhaps, my Lord will grant me (something) better than your garden and send down upon your garden thunderbolts from the sky so that it becomes a flattened plain."
  18,41,Or its water may sink so deep into the ground that you will never be able to obtain it (again).’
  18,42,"(And so it happened.) His fruits were (entirely) destroyed, and he began to wring his hands over what he had invested while it had collapsed on its trellises, and he was saying: ‘I wish I had not ascribed any partner to my Lord.’"
  18,43,"He had no group to help him besides Allah, nor could he help himself."
  18,44,"In this situation, the only protection* is that of Allah, the real (God). He is the best in rewarding and the best in requiting."
  18,45,"Draw an example of this worldly life for them: (It is) like the water We send down from the sky. Then the vegetation of the earth absorbs it (to grow). Then it (i.e. the vegetation) becomes dry, broken into pieces, which the winds scatter (afterwards). And Allah holds power over everything."
